# Audit Log (ticket 04). Log in with http/auth.http, create a Tenant and make it your Active
# Tenant with http/tenants.http: those steps are recorded too. Tenant Admins only.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@accessToken = paste-access-token-with-tid
@userEmail = you@example.com
@cursor = paste-nextCursor

### Newest entries of the Active Tenant's chain
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/audit-events
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Filters combine with AND. "to" is exclusive; "user" is a User ID or email (actor or target).
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/audit-events?from=2026-01-01T00:00:00Z&to=2030-01-01T00:00:00Z&user={{userEmail}}&eventType=tenant.switched&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Next page
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/audit-events?limit=10&cursor={{cursor}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Every event type, for the filter
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/audit-events/types
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Verify the hash chain: { intact, checkedEntries, headSeq, headHash, firstBrokenLink }
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/audit-events/integrity
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

# To see the check fail, change an entry as the postgres superuser (the append-only trigger
# blocks everyone else), then verify again: firstBrokenLink.problem is "hash-mismatch".
#
#   BEGIN; SET LOCAL session_replication_role = replica;
#   UPDATE audit_events SET payload = '{"name":"Evil"}' WHERE "tenantId" = '<tenant id>' AND seq = 1;
#   COMMIT;
#
# Deleting a middle entry gives "missing-entry".

### Platform chain (signup, verification, logins): Platform Admins only, 403 otherwise
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/platform/audit-events
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Platform chain integrity
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/platform/audit-events/integrity
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
